770
00:41:14,340 --> 00:41:15,700
Cut it out!

771
00:41:15,820 --> 00:41:16,580
What are you doing?

772
00:41:16,680 --> 00:41:17,680
That tickles!

773
00:41:20,260 --> 00:41:28,260
Hey, I don't want this on a big-time TV
show.

774
00:41:31,560 --> 00:41:32,560
Okay,

775
00:41:36,480 --> 00:41:38,240
raised your arms up high over your head.

776
00:41:38,360 --> 00:41:38,800
Huh?

777
00:41:38,801 --> 00:41:38,920
Huh?

778
00:41:39,220 --> 00:41:40,220
It's a trust exercise.

779
00:41:40,520 --> 00:41:41,040
Come on!

780
00:41:41,140 --> 00:41:42,140
Raise them high!

781
00:41:44,460 --> 00:41:46,140
Five prong seal release!

782
00:41:55,810 --> 00:42:00,050
What the heck was that for?

783
00:42:00,370 --> 00:42:00,770
What?

784
00:42:01,230 --> 00:42:03,950
Just pushing a pressure point to loosen
you up.

785
00:42:04,670 --> 00:42:05,770
Now, go on.

786
00:42:06,150 --> 00:42:07,630
Try walking on the water again.

787
00:42:16,950 --> 00:42:18,530
Whoa, that's weird!

788
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:27,460
Look at that!

789
00:42:27,540 --> 00:42:28,280
I'm doing it!

790
00:42:28,440 --> 00:42:29,860
Just don't ask me how!

791
00:42:30,080 --> 00:42:31,080
Yahoo!

792
00:42:31,400 --> 00:42:32,400
Look at me!

793
00:42:32,500 --> 00:42:33,240
No problem!

794
00:42:33,320 --> 00:42:34,320
Piece of cake!

795
00:42:35,580 --> 00:42:40,040
I think it's about time to teach him how
to control the fox's chakra.

796
00:42:40,660 --> 00:42:42,140
Okay, out of the pool!

797
00:42:42,660 --> 00:42:43,660
Come on in!

798
00:42:44,010 --> 00:42:45,620
I'm gonna teach you a killer technique.

799
00:42:46,235 --> 00:42:47,000
You are?

800
00:42:47,120 --> 00:42:47,300
You're really?

801
00:42:47,800 --> 00:42:50,180
You mean like something really powerful
and destructive?

802
00:42:55,920 --> 00:43:00,340
Now then, there's something you need to
understand, kid, before we go any further.

803
00:43:01,600 --> 00:43:06,460
I don't think you're even aware of it,
but you possess two chakras within you.

804
00:43:06,980 --> 00:43:07,160
Huh?

805
00:43:07,560 --> 00:43:08,660
Two chakras?

806
00:43:08,900 --> 00:43:11,740
Haven't you ever felt the presence of a
different chakra?

807
00:43:12,660 --> 00:43:14,080
Well, I'm not sure.

808
00:43:15,040 --> 00:43:16,040
Hmm...

809
00:43:18,140 --> 00:43:19,140
Oh, wait!

810
00:43:20,380 --> 00:43:22,000
I do kind of remember.

811
00:43:22,200 --> 00:43:24,300
There was this one time...

812
00:43:24,301 --> 00:43:27,548
It was like all of a sudden
I had this weird upsurge

813
00:43:27,549 --> 00:43:29,900
of power and I didn't
know where it came from.

814
00:43:30,080 --> 00:43:32,420
I don't remember when it was exactly.

815
00:43:32,640 --> 00:43:34,540
I almost thought it was a dream.

816
00:43:35,100 --> 00:43:36,180
So I see.

817
00:43:36,460 --> 00:43:40,600
But I do remember feeling that this was
something different than my usual chakra.

818
00:43:41,380 --> 00:43:42,640
My normal chakra?

819
00:43:44,160 --> 00:43:47,880
Well, if it was a color, it'd be blue.

820
00:43:48,220 --> 00:43:49,700
But this was red.

821
00:43:52,080 --> 00:43:54,440
Okay, that's enough training for today.

822
00:43:54,900 --> 00:43:55,900
What, already?

823
00:43:56,020 --> 00:43:57,340
What about that killer technique?

824
00:43:57,620 --> 00:43:58,500
Come on!

825
00:43:58,501 --> 00:43:59,720
I'm just getting started!

826
00:43:59,740 --> 00:44:00,160
Let's go!

827
00:44:00,300 --> 00:44:03,580
In training as in cooking, a watched pot
never boils.

828
00:44:04,110 --> 00:44:09,380
Now, let's go back to town and have a real
bath, not one where you just fall in, okay?

829
00:44:22,800 --> 00:44:25,080
This is better than falling in.

830
00:44:27,460 --> 00:44:30,760
Nothing beats relaxing after a long day of
training.

831
00:44:31,440 --> 00:44:33,280
Hey, hey, pervy sage!

832
00:44:33,680 --> 00:44:35,440
So tell me about this killer technique.

833
00:44:35,900 --> 00:44:37,400
Tomorrow is soon enough.

834
00:44:37,820 --> 00:44:39,380
Ah, cheapskate!

835
00:44:50,040 --> 00:44:51,500
We'd better get out soon.

836
00:44:51,501 --> 00:44:54,100
Or we're going to be stuck with a giant
boiled toad.

837
00:45:09,330 --> 00:45:10,330
Sorry, Ebisu.

838
00:45:10,720 --> 00:45:13,120
It wasn't my plan to steal your student
from you.

839
00:45:15,930 --> 00:45:17,210
Oh, that's of little importance.

840
00:45:18,190 --> 00:45:20,800
Lord Hokage has had his ninja searching
for you everywhere.

841
00:45:20,801 --> 00:45:23,780
We were just beginning to think that you
would never be found.

842
00:45:24,480 --> 00:45:27,400
Then you turn up here, of all places,
right in front of me.

843
00:45:28,270 --> 00:45:29,270
He will be pleased.

844
00:45:30,500 --> 00:45:32,680
Have you told the Hokage you found me yet?

845
00:45:33,120 --> 00:45:33,600
No.

846
00:45:33,980 --> 00:45:34,980
Not yet.

847
00:45:35,640 --> 00:45:36,640
Very good.

848
00:45:37,160 --> 00:45:38,160
It's better that way.

849
00:45:38,550 --> 00:45:40,240
You're after Orochimaru, aren't you?

850
00:45:40,710 --> 00:45:42,880
No, unfortunately, I can't say that I am.

851
00:45:42,940 --> 00:45:43,240
Sorry.

852
00:45:43,840 --> 00:45:44,840
Huh?

853
00:45:45,030 --> 00:45:48,880
The only thing that brought me here was the
chance of doing some research for a book.

854
00:45:48,881 --> 00:45:52,360
I have no desire to get involved in any of
that other business.

855
00:45:52,720 --> 00:45:53,420
What do you mean?

856
00:45:53,500 --> 00:45:54,500
You can't be serious!

857
00:45:54,980 --> 00:45:56,200
You know better than anyone!

858
00:45:57,230 --> 00:45:59,100
There's only one way to deal with
Orochimaru.

859
00:45:59,450 --> 00:46:02,240
He's one of the Sannin, the legendary
three ninja.

860
00:46:02,480 --> 00:46:05,200
And he can only be stopped by the power of
another Sannin!

861
00:46:05,780 --> 00:46:07,380
Your power, Master Jiraiya!

862
00:46:30,590 --> 00:46:32,590
Don't you ever sleep at all?

863
00:46:33,850 --> 00:46:35,150
Why are you here?

864
00:46:35,230 --> 00:46:35,890
What do you want?

865
00:46:35,891 --> 00:46:39,750
I was planning on attacking you while you
slept.

866
00:46:40,070 --> 00:46:43,330
I already know all about your sand attack.

867
00:46:43,730 --> 00:46:50,010
I wonder which is faster, your sand or my
sound?

868
00:46:54,510 --> 00:47:03,130
When the moon is full... When
the moon is full, its blood boils.

869
00:47:08,790 --> 00:47:11,190
What in the world are you?

870
00:47:23,000 --> 00:47:24,000
Amazing.

871
00:47:24,120 --> 00:47:26,860
So that's Gaara's true form, then,
is it?

872
00:47:29,460 --> 00:47:30,920
I can't believe it.

873
00:47:31,000 --> 00:47:33,440
A tailed beast brought into this village.

874
00:47:36,180 --> 00:47:39,240
Well, there's certainly no denying its
power.

875
00:47:39,580 --> 00:47:42,080
But are you actually able to control it?

876
00:47:42,540 --> 00:47:44,000
At that level, yes.

877
00:47:44,001 --> 00:47:47,209
But when the one tail transforms
completely and activates

878
00:47:47,210 --> 00:47:50,460
his playing possum jutsu,
there's no stopping him.

879
00:47:50,680 --> 00:47:51,800
All right, fine.

880
00:47:52,060 --> 00:47:54,640
Then we'd better not agitate him any
further for now.

881
00:47:54,900 --> 00:47:58,200
But I look forward to seeing him run amok
when the time finally comes.

882
00:47:58,580 --> 00:48:00,080
Listen, is this okay?

883
00:48:00,300 --> 00:48:01,340
He was a sound ninja.

884
00:48:01,600 --> 00:48:02,760
Yes, it's fine.

885
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:04,780
He's long since served his purpose.

886
00:48:05,720 --> 00:48:10,620
But I thought he was a guinea pig intended
to test the power of that kid, Sasuke.

887
00:48:11,340 --> 00:48:11,860
What?

888
00:48:12,040 --> 00:48:13,980
Is Kabuto in league with the sand ninja?

889
00:48:15,140 --> 00:48:15,920
That's true.

890
00:48:16,100 --> 00:48:16,840
Or it was.

891
00:48:16,900 --> 00:48:18,160
It isn't necessary anymore.

892
00:48:18,860 --> 00:48:22,940
See, the thing is, I was ordered to see
Sasuke when he was in the hospital.

893
00:48:23,410 --> 00:48:25,640
But I... well, I failed in that mission.

894
00:48:26,520 --> 00:48:27,520
Wait, what?

895
00:48:27,560 --> 00:48:28,560
Yes, that's right.

896
00:48:28,720 --> 00:48:31,380
They've discovered that I'm an agent of
the Sound Village.

897
00:48:31,940 --> 00:48:35,640
I thought you were Orochimaru's right-hand
man.

898
00:48:36,060 --> 00:48:40,480
But after being revealed to them, you just
nonchalantly come here and meet with me?

899
00:48:40,940 --> 00:48:41,940
You're a fool.

900
00:48:42,320 --> 00:48:42,700
Heh heh.

901
00:48:42,701 --> 00:48:45,100
I let them find out.

902
00:48:45,680 --> 00:48:48,680
Yes, I wanted to see just
how far the Hidden Leaf

903
00:48:48,681 --> 00:48:51,181
Village would go when
they discovered the truth.

904
00:48:51,360 --> 00:48:55,340
And even after they did, I knew it
wouldn't be too late to seize Sasuke.

905
00:48:56,360 --> 00:49:01,400
It's a plan that was originally posed by
the Sound Village, so... if you guys are

906
00:49:01,401 --> 00:49:03,900
gonna fail, then we'll have to back off
immediately.

907
00:49:04,960 --> 00:49:05,960
Hmph.

908
00:49:07,230 --> 00:49:09,420
The sand won't make a move till the last
moment.

909
00:49:10,500 --> 00:49:12,620
This is the will of the Kazekai.

910
00:49:14,070 --> 00:49:15,070
This can't be!

911
00:49:15,780 --> 00:49:16,780
Very well.

912
00:49:18,320 --> 00:49:20,180
This is the plan that you're to carry out.

913
00:49:21,140 --> 00:49:22,140
Okay.

914
00:49:23,590 --> 00:49:27,840
And remember, make sure you tell them
about this plan as soon as possible.

915
00:49:29,500 --> 00:49:30,500
Yes.

916
00:49:30,900 --> 00:49:31,900
I know.

917
00:49:34,560 --> 00:49:35,560
All right.

918
00:49:36,380 --> 00:49:37,380
Then I'll be going.

919
00:49:38,310 --> 00:49:42,240
To think our ally, the Sand Village,
has a secret pact with the Sound Village!

920
00:49:42,241 --> 00:49:44,640
I must tell Lord Hokage!

921
00:49:45,780 --> 00:49:47,900
I'll take care of our little spy.

922
00:49:49,180 --> 00:49:50,180
No, wait.

923
00:49:50,440 --> 00:49:51,920
I will handle this.

924
00:49:52,080 --> 00:49:55,062
As a gesture of faith
in our allegiance, the

925
00:49:55,063 --> 00:49:58,561
least we Sand Ninja can
do is lend a helping hand.

926
00:49:59,040 --> 00:50:02,040
Besides, it's just one little spy.

927
00:50:02,540 --> 00:50:03,740
It'll be easy.

928
00:50:04,460 --> 00:50:06,041
... ...

929
00:50:06,360 --> 00:50:07,941
... ...

930
00:50:12,920 --> 00:50:14,621
Grrr... Grrr...

931
00:50:22,660 --> 00:50:24,060
Aahhh!

932
00:50:24,480 --> 00:50:25,480
Achoo!

933
00:50:25,560 --> 00:50:26,760
Ahhhhh!

934
00:50:27,500 --> 00:50:29,901
Ha... Ha...

935
00:51:05,400 --> 00:51:06,760
This is unexpected.

936
00:51:07,340 --> 00:51:10,060
I thought that this fight would be settled
almost immediately.

937
00:51:11,000 --> 00:51:15,860
I have to say, that Proctor was very slick
to slip past me the way he did.

938
00:51:20,140 --> 00:51:21,220
Sheathing your sword.

939
00:51:22,180 --> 00:51:23,180
Now!

940
00:51:26,220 --> 00:51:28,560
Leaf-style crescent moon death!

941
00:51:38,160 --> 00:51:39,620
My sword's stuck!

942
00:51:39,920 --> 00:51:41,740
Your talent with a sword is superb.

943
00:51:42,100 --> 00:51:46,220
Of course, stopping a physical sword is
easy and is only a rudimentary skill.

944
00:51:47,020 --> 00:51:48,020
However...

945
00:51:48,840 --> 00:51:51,180
A wind sword is a different story.

946
00:51:51,340 --> 00:51:52,800
No one can stop it.

947
00:51:55,680 --> 00:51:56,680
Ah!

948
00:52:17,360 --> 00:52:19,040
We got you!

949
00:52:21,920 --> 00:52:22,920
Oh!

950
00:52:24,640 --> 00:52:25,640
Wow!

951
00:52:25,760 --> 00:52:26,760
Good on you!

952
00:52:27,320 --> 00:52:28,560
Knock it off!

953
00:52:29,260 --> 00:52:30,980
Alright, Naruto.

954
00:52:31,420 --> 00:52:33,580
I guess I'll teach you a technique now.

955
00:52:33,860 --> 00:52:37,040
Well, it's about time and you better not
be kidding around here.

956
00:52:38,820 --> 00:52:41,660
Okay, do you remember what we talked about
yesterday?

957
00:52:41,980 --> 00:52:44,280
You know, that stuff about the two types
of chakra?

958
00:52:44,640 --> 00:52:44,800
Huh?

959
00:52:45,190 --> 00:52:46,190
We talked yesterday?

960
00:52:46,510 --> 00:52:47,510
Very funny.

961
00:52:47,665 --> 00:52:50,120
Remember you said something about having
different chakra?

962
00:52:50,320 --> 00:52:51,600
One blue and one red?

963
00:52:51,880 --> 00:52:52,640
Oh, yeah.

964
00:52:52,780 --> 00:52:53,780
So what about it?

965
00:52:54,710 --> 00:52:58,900
You said that when you exerted enormous
strength, you felt red chakra.

966
00:52:59,320 --> 00:53:00,220
Yeah, that's right.

967
00:53:00,300 --> 00:53:01,940
I don't know how else to describe it.

968
00:53:02,340 --> 00:53:05,540
Alright, try building up that red chakra
right now.

969
00:53:06,080 --> 00:53:07,080
Right now?

970
00:53:07,930 --> 00:53:09,440
Well, I guess if you say so.

971
00:53:10,509 --> 00:53:11,940
Okay, I'll give it a try.

972
00:53:21,130 --> 00:53:22,130
Well, did it work?

973
00:53:23,424 --> 00:53:24,840
No, it's not right.

974
00:53:25,020 --> 00:53:26,820
It's the same chakra as always.

975
00:53:27,520 --> 00:53:31,000
Oh, man, you really have absolute zero
talent, don't you, kid?

976
00:53:31,230 --> 00:53:33,220
Hey, don't go acting like you're so great.

977
00:53:33,480 --> 00:53:35,160
And besides, I can't help it.

978
00:53:35,200 --> 00:53:38,360
I mean, I don't even understand those two
types of chakra myself, alright?

979
00:53:38,640 --> 00:53:40,340
Just keep trying.

980
00:53:41,849 --> 00:53:42,660
I'm just trying.

981
00:53:42,661 --> 00:53:43,300
Fine, I will.

982
00:53:43,569 --> 00:53:44,280
Hmm.

983
00:53:44,580 --> 00:53:47,160
So he doesn't understand it, huh?

984
00:53:48,100 --> 00:53:50,996
Naruto probably still
hasn't realized that his

985
00:53:50,997 --> 00:53:54,361
red chakra is really the
nine-tailed fox's chakra.

986
00:53:55,220 --> 00:54:00,220
Judging by his story, it seems that the
excitement caused by danger and also

987
00:54:00,221 --> 00:54:03,920
strong emotion are the keys to summoning
the nine-tailed fox chakra.

988
00:54:05,820 --> 00:54:07,180
It's just no good.

989
00:54:07,280 --> 00:54:10,060
I'm only getting the usual everyday chakra
here.

990
00:54:10,640 --> 00:54:12,060
Hey, hold on a second.

991
00:54:12,240 --> 00:54:14,420
Maybe I don't even need to summon the red
chakra.

992
00:54:14,600 --> 00:54:16,293
I mean, what in the world
does it have to do with

993
00:54:16,294 --> 00:54:18,581
the technique that you're
gonna teach me anyway?

994
00:54:19,380 --> 00:54:20,380
Listen, boy.

995
00:54:21,920 --> 00:54:24,662
For the technique I'm going
to teach you, the chakra

996
00:54:24,663 --> 00:54:27,440
you've used until now is
nowhere near powerful enough.

997
00:54:28,960 --> 00:54:32,620
If you want to use this technique,
you'll have to be able to pull out all the

998
00:54:32,621 --> 00:54:35,328
stops and tap into the other
chakra that's been dormant

999
00:54:35,329 --> 00:54:37,661
within you, summoning
it up at a moment's notice.

1000
00:54:38,880 --> 00:54:40,320
Yeah, that sounds really good.

1001
00:54:40,340 --> 00:54:41,895
Cool and exciting, but
how do you even know

1002
00:54:41,896 --> 00:54:44,801
that I really have that
chakra inside of me?

1003
00:54:45,120 --> 00:54:47,300
Oh, that's just what I wanted to hear.

1004
00:54:47,860 --> 00:54:51,220
Actually, it's because I am a sage.

1005
00:54:53,540 --> 00:54:56,800
Talk about giving an answer without giving
an answer.

1006
00:54:57,080 --> 00:55:00,960
Anyway, the special chakra that only you
have will become your greatest weapon,

1007
00:55:01,100 --> 00:55:02,100
I am sure of it.

1008
00:55:02,620 --> 00:55:03,420
Greatest weapon?

1009
00:55:03,600 --> 00:55:04,020
Really?

1010
00:55:04,360 --> 00:55:07,160
Yes, not using that is like wasting
treasure.

1011
00:55:07,420 --> 00:55:10,160
Look, there's no need to blindly follow
the same training.

1012
00:55:16,200 --> 00:55:19,500
You have two types of chakra, and don't
exhaust easily.

1013
00:55:19,760 --> 00:55:24,060
So you should learn to release the largest
amount of chakra you can, and then train

1014
00:55:24,061 --> 00:55:27,660
yourself so you can increase the total
amount of chakra you can use.

1015
00:55:28,540 --> 00:55:32,260
Once you do that, a whole world of jutsu
will open up to you.

1016
00:55:34,400 --> 00:55:34,880
Seriously?

1017
00:55:35,230 --> 00:55:36,120
Like what could I do?

1018
00:55:36,121 --> 00:55:40,580
Well, for example, the Summoning Jutsu
that I'm going to teach you.

1019
00:55:43,760 --> 00:55:44,760
Summoning?

1020
00:55:45,020 --> 00:55:46,020
That's right.

1021
00:55:47,639 --> 00:55:52,260
It is a teleportation technique in which
you sign a contract in blood with all

1022
00:55:52,261 --> 00:55:55,034
kinds of living creatures,
and then summon them

1023
00:55:55,035 --> 00:55:57,981
whenever you like with
Ninjutsu, your ninja art.

1024
00:55:58,420 --> 00:55:59,420
Oh yeah!

1025
00:55:59,580 --> 00:56:00,580
That sounds awesome!

1026
00:56:00,680 --> 00:56:01,160
Teach me quick!

1027
00:56:01,220 --> 00:56:01,960
Come on, right now!

1028
00:56:02,020 --> 00:56:03,020
Let's get going already!

1029
00:56:04,480 --> 00:56:05,720
Okay, just relax.

1030
00:56:06,120 --> 00:56:08,796
Before we begin, you're
going to need to use up all

1031
00:56:08,797 --> 00:56:11,381
your usual chakra so just
your red chakra remains.

1032
00:56:11,950 --> 00:56:13,000
All right!

1033
00:56:15,274 --> 00:56:16,480
Leave it to me!

1034
00:56:22,800 --> 00:56:25,980
So, he already knows the Shadow Clone
Jutsu.

1035
00:56:27,220 --> 00:56:28,220
Listen up!

1036
00:56:28,280 --> 00:56:31,360
All of us are going to have one great big
battle royale!

1037
00:56:31,520 --> 00:56:34,820
The last one left standing will be the
strongest me!

1038
00:56:34,821 --> 00:56:37,700
We're going to determine the me among me!

1039
00:56:37,880 --> 00:56:38,420
Get it?

1040
00:56:38,500 --> 00:56:39,500
Yeah!

1041
00:56:39,640 --> 00:56:41,240
Ah, now I see.

1042
00:56:41,890 --> 00:56:44,660
That's a pretty clever idea considering
he's so dumb.

1043
00:56:46,980 --> 00:56:47,980
Ah!

1044
00:56:50,020 --> 00:56:51,020
Ah!

1045
00:56:51,360 --> 00:56:52,360
Ah!

1046
00:56:52,430 --> 00:56:53,430
Ah!

1047
00:56:53,600 --> 00:56:54,280
Ah!

1048
00:56:54,281 --> 00:56:54,680
Ah!

1049
00:56:54,681 --> 00:56:55,681
Ah!

1050
00:56:55,840 --> 00:56:56,520
Ah!

1051
00:56:56,521 --> 00:56:56,580
Ah!

1052
00:56:56,581 --> 00:56:56,760
Ah!

1053
00:56:56,761 --> 00:56:57,160
Ah!

1054
00:56:57,161 --> 00:56:58,161
Ah!

1055
00:56:58,375 --> 00:56:59,375
Ah!

1056
00:57:08,995 --> 00:57:13,080
It seems that at long last you've finally
used up almost all your usual chakra.

1057
00:57:14,250 --> 00:57:16,440
Now I can teach you the technique.

1058
00:57:17,020 --> 00:57:17,480
Yes!

1059
00:57:17,481 --> 00:57:19,500
Oh man, I've been waiting for this all
day!

1060
00:57:19,880 --> 00:57:20,680
I couldn't tell.

1061
00:57:20,880 --> 00:57:22,960
All right, first I'm going to show you how
it's done.

1062
00:57:23,110 --> 00:57:24,740
Now watch carefully.

1063
00:57:28,920 --> 00:57:29,920
Summoning Jutsu!

1064
00:57:36,160 --> 00:57:38,360
Whoa, that is totally awesome!

1065
00:57:38,780 --> 00:57:40,900
That may be the coolest thing ever!

1066
00:57:44,820 --> 00:57:45,820
Go

1067
00:57:52,990 --> 00:57:55,170
ahead, open that scroll and take a look
inside.

1068
00:57:55,710 --> 00:57:58,086
It's a contract with the
summoning toads that's

1069
00:57:58,087 --> 00:58:00,790
been handed down from
earlier generations of ninja.

1070
00:58:01,990 --> 00:58:05,178
Just sign your name in your
own blood and stamp the

1071
00:58:05,179 --> 00:58:07,930
fingerprints of one hand in
blood beneath your signature.

1072
00:58:09,150 --> 00:58:11,650
Find the place where you want to summon
the creature.

1073
00:58:11,651 --> 00:58:15,250
Then build up chakra and press down the
hand you used on the contract.

1074
00:58:15,970 --> 00:58:19,690
That seal is Ino I Torisaru Itsuchi.

1075
00:58:25,250 --> 00:58:29,350
Here goes Naruto Uzumaki!

1076
00:58:42,570 --> 00:58:44,290
Okay, I'm all done, right?

1077
00:58:44,430 --> 00:58:45,430
What's next?

1078
00:58:45,750 --> 00:58:47,891
After burning off
your regular chakra, it

1079
00:58:47,892 --> 00:58:50,470
should be easier to
release your red chakra now.

1080
00:58:50,810 --> 00:58:51,990
So give it a try.

1081
00:58:52,890 --> 00:58:54,950
Quit bugging me, I already am!

1082
00:58:55,190 --> 00:58:59,030
Okay, Ino, I, Tori, Saru, Itsuchi...

1083
00:59:00,590 --> 00:59:02,630
Ninja Art Summoning Jutsu!

1084
00:59:09,750 --> 00:59:11,030
A tadpole?

1085
00:59:11,850 --> 00:59:14,830
Sure enough, this kid has no talent
whatsoever.

1086
00:59:33,010 --> 00:59:35,790
Hayate, what in the world happened to you?

1087
00:59:39,110 --> 00:59:40,110
Hey,

1088
00:59:51,580 --> 00:59:53,300
let's see how you like it!

1089
00:59:55,920 --> 00:59:58,300
Hey, Kirby Sage, hello!

1090
00:59:58,880 --> 01:00:01,860
Are you going to watch me try this jutsu
again or not?

1091
01:00:02,060 --> 01:00:04,540
Can't you see I'm busy with my research?

1092
01:00:04,840 --> 01:00:05,840
Do it yourself!

1093
01:00:06,480 --> 01:00:11,540
Okay, I will, and this time I'm going to
summon a frog the size of a house!

1094
01:00:15,320 --> 01:00:16,400
Summoning Jutsu!

1095
01:00:21,120 --> 01:00:21,520
Wait!

1096
01:00:21,521 --> 01:00:23,460
Give it a second, I think it's still
growing!

1097
01:00:23,820 --> 01:00:26,900
Listen, if you're not going to take this
seriously, then I'm through with you!

1098
01:00:26,940 --> 01:00:27,960
Do you understand me?

1099
01:00:28,280 --> 01:00:29,280
I am serious!

1100
01:00:29,340 --> 01:00:31,660
You're the one who's staring at the girls,
you old goat!

1101
01:00:31,780 --> 01:00:35,240
Stop fooling around and focus on your
chakras if your life depended on it!

1102
01:00:35,360 --> 01:00:36,860
What do you think I'm doing?

1103
01:00:42,855 --> 01:00:45,100
Some of you may not yet have heard the
news.

1104
01:00:45,101 --> 01:00:49,660
The body of Hayate Gekko was found near
Kikyo Castle.

1105
01:00:50,480 --> 01:00:51,080
What?

1106
01:00:51,200 --> 01:00:52,200
Hayate?

1107
01:00:52,230 --> 01:00:53,400
He's... he's dead?

1108
01:00:53,780 --> 01:00:54,780
Unbelievable.

1109
01:00:55,610 --> 01:00:57,960
This has to be Orochimaru's doing.

1110
01:00:58,220 --> 01:01:01,820
As likely as that may seem, let's not jump
to conclusions yet.

1111
01:01:01,920 --> 01:01:06,100
We think Hayate was on the trail of a
sound village spy named Kabuto.

1112
01:01:06,460 --> 01:01:11,020
No doubt Orochimaru is up to something,
but we don't know for sure if...

1113
01:01:11,021 --> 01:01:14,120
What I say, cancel the tuning exams and go
after Orochimaru.

1114
01:01:15,160 --> 01:01:16,680
No, I think not.

1115
01:01:17,020 --> 01:01:21,580
He revealed himself to Anka and sent a
warning not to cancel the exams.

1116
01:01:22,000 --> 01:01:26,760
You see, these exams have brought together
ninja from every allied nation.

1117
01:01:27,360 --> 01:01:28,680
What do you think it means?

1118
01:01:29,640 --> 01:01:31,740
There are two things we know about him.

1119
01:01:31,820 --> 01:01:34,151
That he bears an abiding
grudge against our

1120
01:01:34,152 --> 01:01:37,041
Hidden Leaf Village, and
that his power is great.

1121
01:01:37,200 --> 01:01:40,020
Perhaps great enough to crush a village on
his own.

1122
01:01:40,840 --> 01:01:44,720
Certainly great enough that any village
would prefer to have him on their side.

1123
01:01:44,760 --> 01:01:45,080
Certainly great enough that any village
would prefer to have him on their side.

1124
01:01:45,081 --> 01:01:46,820
Rather than against them.

1125
01:01:47,520 --> 01:01:48,160
Impossible!

1126
01:01:48,520 --> 01:01:53,200
No village in the Alliance would betray
another and join forces with that fiend!

1127
01:01:54,000 --> 01:01:58,580
Well, the Alliance Treaty is only as
binding as any verbal agreement.

1128
01:01:59,280 --> 01:02:02,780
As we found out during the last Great
Ninja War.

1129
01:02:03,300 --> 01:02:10,260
In any case, until we're able to find out
more, this is all just idle speculation.

1130
01:02:10,880 --> 01:02:14,800
We've dispatched Anbu Black Ops to every
village to collect information.

1131
01:02:14,801 --> 01:02:17,660
We would be fools to act too hastily.

1132
01:02:17,840 --> 01:02:20,880
That might be just what our enemy is
aiming for.

1133
01:02:22,440 --> 01:02:23,680
And besides...

1134
01:02:24,540 --> 01:02:27,735
When and if the time comes,
we will gather the strength

1135
01:02:27,736 --> 01:02:31,480
of the Hidden Leaf
Village and fight if we must.

1136
01:02:37,460 --> 01:02:39,130
That's right, I should bring flowers!

1137
01:02:43,650 --> 01:02:45,590
Let's see now...

1138
01:02:49,490 --> 01:02:52,960
Oh no... Oh, Sakura,
you poor thing.

1139
01:02:53,080 --> 01:02:55,800
It's sad when a girl has to buy flowers
for herself.

1140
01:02:56,360 --> 01:02:57,360
I'm not!

1141
01:02:57,780 --> 01:03:00,420
I'm, uh... Not that it's
any of your business.

1142
01:03:00,600 --> 01:03:02,980
I didn't expect to find you minding the
shop.

1143
01:03:04,340 --> 01:03:05,520
I'll make this quick.

1144
01:03:06,900 --> 01:03:09,231
Taking a planter to the
hospital is like saying

1145
01:03:09,232 --> 01:03:11,260
you expect the person
to be there forever.

1146
01:03:11,540 --> 01:03:13,780
Some cut flowers might be a better idea.

1147
01:03:14,060 --> 01:03:15,060
Um...

1148
01:03:15,320 --> 01:03:15,800
Hospital?

1149
01:03:16,200 --> 01:03:16,880
What do you mean?

1150
01:03:17,160 --> 01:03:18,540
Don't play dumb with me.

1151
01:03:18,541 --> 01:03:21,480
You're going there to visit Sasuke,
aren't you?

1152
01:03:21,940 --> 01:03:24,680
Hey, Mom!

1153
01:03:25,420 --> 01:03:26,880
I'm going out for a while.

1154
01:03:27,660 --> 01:03:29,220
Wait, what are you doing?

1155
01:03:29,380 --> 01:03:29,780
Get real.

1156
01:03:29,960 --> 01:03:32,980
If you think I'm gonna let you be the
first one to get in to see Sasuke,

1157
01:03:33,140 --> 01:03:35,920
you are so wrong.

1158
01:03:37,240 --> 01:03:39,780
Miss Ino-Pig, always butting in!

1159
01:03:41,460 --> 01:03:43,640
I think I'll bring him one red rose.

1160
01:03:44,040 --> 01:03:45,660
It's the flower of love.

1161
01:03:46,600 --> 01:03:47,080
Ha!

1162
01:03:47,081 --> 01:03:48,660
How lame can you get?

1163
01:03:49,080 --> 01:03:49,560
Me?

1164
01:03:49,760 --> 01:03:52,000
I'm gonna bring him a single daffodil.

1165
01:03:52,500 --> 01:03:55,964
A noble flower that bravely
endures the long months

1166
01:03:55,965 --> 01:03:58,861
of winter, then blossoms
forth as a sign of spring.

1167
01:03:59,460 --> 01:04:02,560
Just like you will soon blossom again,
Sasuke.

1168
01:04:03,554 --> 01:04:05,860
What are you, a botanist all of a sudden?

1169
01:04:06,080 --> 01:04:08,200
I warned you I will not lose out to you!

1170
01:04:08,500 --> 01:04:08,980
Whatever.

1171
01:04:09,380 --> 01:04:11,420
So are you gonna pay for that daffodil?

1172
01:04:11,620 --> 01:04:13,100
I should get two.

1173
01:04:13,440 --> 01:04:13,920
Two?

1174
01:04:14,000 --> 01:04:14,300
Why?

1175
01:04:14,301 --> 01:04:15,840
You trying to impress him?

1176
01:04:16,435 --> 01:04:18,440
One for him, and another for Lee.

1177
01:04:21,904 --> 01:04:22,550
Later!

1178
01:04:22,870 --> 01:04:23,870
More!

1179
01:04:25,330 --> 01:04:27,030
Ten orders of short ribs!

1180
01:04:31,730 --> 01:04:34,370
Man, you can put me off of food for good.

1181
01:04:34,630 --> 01:04:36,690
Just watching you makes me sick.

1182
01:04:36,930 --> 01:04:38,470
So, did you order the short ribs?

1183
01:04:39,150 --> 01:04:40,190
Ah, finally!

1184
01:04:42,850 --> 01:04:44,910
This is all mine, Shikamaru!

1185
01:04:44,911 --> 01:04:46,210
Don't try stealing any!

1186
01:04:46,970 --> 01:04:49,030
Don't worry, I wasn't planning on it.

1187
01:04:51,570 --> 01:04:53,430
What the heck are you guys doing?

1188
01:04:53,850 --> 01:04:54,850
Huh?

1189
01:04:54,890 --> 01:04:55,450
Ino!

1190
01:04:55,451 --> 01:04:56,451
Sakura!

1191
01:04:56,630 --> 01:04:58,665
Shikamaru, shouldn't
you be training for the

1192
01:04:58,666 --> 01:05:01,110
final exam instead of
sitting around pigging out?

1193
01:05:01,370 --> 01:05:02,550
I have been training.

1194
01:05:02,750 --> 01:05:04,370
Every day, all day.

1195
01:05:04,990 --> 01:05:06,970
Asuma's a goddamn slave driver.

1196
01:05:08,450 --> 01:05:10,750
And it's not only Shikamaru.

1197
01:05:10,930 --> 01:05:12,950
Choji's joined us for training as well.

1198
01:05:13,230 --> 01:05:14,230
What?

1199
01:05:14,910 --> 01:05:16,650
So you're going for it after all,
huh?

1200
01:05:16,950 --> 01:05:17,410
Mm-hmm!

1201
01:05:17,690 --> 01:05:18,690
Yeah!

1202
01:05:19,030 --> 01:05:21,970
And in return, I get all the barbecue I
can eat!

1203
01:05:22,130 --> 01:05:23,630
Well, that would explain it.

1204
01:05:23,850 --> 01:05:24,850
Oh, man.

1205
01:05:25,190 --> 01:05:28,770
I wish I'd never signed up for this stupid
final exam.

1206
01:05:28,950 --> 01:05:30,030
I don't want to hear it.

1207
01:05:30,090 --> 01:05:33,090
There are plenty of people who'd give
their right arm to be a part of it.

1208
01:05:33,210 --> 01:05:35,720
And besides, from
everything I've heard, Guy and

1209
01:05:35,721 --> 01:05:38,230
Kurenai's teams are
training their butts off.

1210
01:05:38,490 --> 01:05:39,490
Yeah?

1211
01:05:39,550 --> 01:05:40,570
Well, what about it?

1212
01:05:40,750 --> 01:05:42,210
After coming this far.

1213
01:05:42,211 --> 01:05:45,090
You don't want them making you look bad,
do you?

1214
01:05:47,570 --> 01:05:49,810
Man, this is such a drag.

1215
01:05:56,550 --> 01:05:58,130
I can't keep this up.

1216
01:05:58,420 --> 01:05:59,590
No human being could.

1217
01:06:00,390 --> 01:06:02,490
Think I've used too much of my chakra.

1218
01:06:04,610 --> 01:06:05,170
Neji!

1219
01:06:05,410 --> 01:06:06,410
Are you alright?

1220
01:06:41,280 --> 01:06:42,280
I'm alright.

1221
01:06:44,420 --> 01:06:46,180
I'll get with the tadpoles!

1222
01:06:46,340 --> 01:06:48,320
This is ridiculous, we're not getting
anywhere!

1223
01:06:48,660 --> 01:06:48,920
Look!

1224
01:06:49,280 --> 01:06:50,240
Can't you see it?

1225
01:06:50,260 --> 01:06:51,800
This one's bigger than the last one!

1226
01:06:52,080 --> 01:06:53,240
Who cares?!

1227
01:06:53,241 --> 01:06:54,840
It's still a tadpole!

1228
01:06:55,380 --> 01:06:56,380
Hahaha!

1229
01:07:01,080 --> 01:07:02,780
So you're here to see Sasuke Uchiha?

1230
01:07:03,890 --> 01:07:06,340
Please keep in mind that he's still very
weak.

1231
01:07:06,765 --> 01:07:07,765
He needs his rest.

1232
01:07:08,590 --> 01:07:10,180
You'll have to keep your visit short.

1233
01:07:10,420 --> 01:07:12,340
Five minutes, that's all I can give you.

1234
01:07:12,600 --> 01:07:13,600
All right.

1235
01:07:15,400 --> 01:07:15,840
Sasuke?

1236
01:07:15,890 --> 01:07:16,890
May I come in?

1237
01:07:17,100 --> 01:07:19,120
You have a couple of pretty visitors here.

1238
01:07:23,360 --> 01:07:23,800
Sasuke?

1239
01:07:23,801 --> 01:07:24,801
Sasuke!

1240
01:07:27,775 --> 01:07:28,940
All of his clothes are gone!

1241
01:07:29,140 --> 01:07:29,300
Huh?

1242
01:07:29,840 --> 01:07:30,840
This is terrible!

1243
01:07:30,960 --> 01:07:33,280
He's in no condition to be walking around
on his own!

1244
01:07:33,640 --> 01:07:34,080
Doctor!

1245
01:07:34,480 --> 01:07:34,920
Doctor!

1246
01:07:34,921 --> 01:07:36,440
Oh, Sasuke.

1247
01:07:36,740 --> 01:07:38,060
Where have you gone?

1248
01:07:52,310 --> 01:07:53,310
Huh?

1249
01:07:57,790 --> 01:07:58,790
What's up?

1250
01:07:59,970 --> 01:08:02,090
So you finally showed up.

1251
01:08:08,360 --> 01:08:09,520
Kakashi-sensei!

1252
01:08:09,660 --> 01:08:11,100
I want your help!

1253
01:08:11,180 --> 01:08:12,180
I need to get stronger!

1254
01:08:16,819 --> 01:08:17,439
Hmm.

1255
01:08:17,440 --> 01:08:21,979
This determination of Sasuke's... He's
dead serious.

1256
01:08:23,359 --> 01:08:24,359
It's Naruto.

1257
01:08:24,640 --> 01:08:26,760
He became so strong so fast.

1258
01:08:27,060 --> 01:08:28,920
I just can't waste any more time.

1259
01:08:30,040 --> 01:08:31,060
I see.

1260
01:08:31,479 --> 01:08:32,740
So that's it.

1261
01:08:33,080 --> 01:08:37,640
He finally took notice of the immense
power that Naruto has at his disposal.

1262
01:08:38,380 --> 01:08:39,720
I have a goal.

1263
01:08:39,819 --> 01:08:42,279
And to achieve it, I need to have more
power.

1264
01:08:42,899 --> 01:08:43,520
Okay.

1265
01:08:43,521 --> 01:08:46,201
Well, Sasuke, you know
about the five types of

1266
01:08:46,202 --> 01:08:49,221
chakra and about change
in chakra nature, right?

1267
01:08:49,319 --> 01:08:49,560
Yeah.

1268
01:08:50,040 --> 01:08:52,665
Members of the Uchiha
clan most often possess

1269
01:08:52,666 --> 01:08:56,061
fire nature and
specialize in fire style.

1270
01:08:56,359 --> 01:08:57,819
I already know that.

1271
01:08:57,920 --> 01:08:58,920
What's this about?

1272
01:08:59,300 --> 01:09:03,479
Some shinobi are able to affect more than
one change in chakra nature.

1273
01:09:03,920 --> 01:09:05,899
My chakra nature is lightning.

1274
01:09:08,279 --> 01:09:13,240
Sasuke, for a long time now I've had a
suspicion that you may be similar to me.

1275
01:09:14,380 --> 01:09:17,960
First, I'd like to verify what your chakra
nature is.

1276
01:09:21,160 --> 01:09:25,080
Looks like I may be able to pass my jutsu
onto you after all.

1277
01:09:26,979 --> 01:09:30,500
The unique jutsu of Kakashi the copy
ninja.

1278
01:09:33,960 --> 01:09:34,260
Lee?

1279
01:09:34,570 --> 01:09:35,420
Can we come in?

1280
01:09:35,560 --> 01:09:37,939
You have a couple of pretty visitors here.

1281
01:09:38,450 --> 01:09:39,520
Oh no!

1282
01:09:41,359 --> 01:09:42,779
Not Lee too!

1283
01:09:43,240 --> 01:09:43,899
Lee!

1284
01:09:44,260 --> 01:09:45,260
Lee!

1285
01:09:45,420 --> 01:09:46,420
Weird.

1286
01:09:46,880 --> 01:09:47,880
Huh?

1287
01:09:48,520 --> 01:09:49,100
Look!

1288
01:09:49,359 --> 01:09:50,359
Huh?

1289
01:09:55,910 --> 01:09:57,830
200 push-ups, that was the deal!

1290
01:09:57,970 --> 01:10:01,910
If you cannot finish them, it is 100 leg
squats, so come on!

1291
01:10:02,130 --> 01:10:03,170
Here we go!

1292
01:10:04,470 --> 01:10:05,470
190...

1293
01:10:09,205 --> 01:10:10,205
Lee!

1294
01:10:11,210 --> 01:10:12,530
You shouldn't be out of bed!

1295
01:10:12,810 --> 01:10:13,610
Stop it!

1296
01:10:13,611 --> 01:10:15,310
What do you think you're doing?

1297
01:10:16,510 --> 01:10:17,510
191...

1298
01:10:18,910 --> 01:10:19,550
Lee!

1299
01:10:19,770 --> 01:10:21,010
Keep away from me!

1300
01:10:22,610 --> 01:10:23,610
Please!

1301
01:10:24,150 --> 01:10:27,330
Got to... finish my training!

1302
01:10:29,870 --> 01:10:31,630
I should get two.

1303
01:10:32,490 --> 01:10:33,130
Two?

1304
01:10:33,170 --> 01:10:33,570
Why?

1305
01:10:33,710 --> 01:10:34,990
You trying to impress him?

1306
01:10:35,630 --> 01:10:38,090
One for him and another for Lee.

1307
01:10:38,450 --> 01:10:39,450
Oh...

1308
01:10:43,570 --> 01:10:47,090
Sakura, speaking of Lee, you heard the
news about him, didn't you?

1309
01:10:47,390 --> 01:10:47,950
Huh?

1310
01:10:48,150 --> 01:10:49,290
What news is that?

1311
01:10:49,690 --> 01:10:51,270
His injuries were bad.

1312
01:10:51,590 --> 01:10:52,590
Really bad.

1313
01:10:52,910 --> 01:10:59,070
It means that he'll never... well,
his days as a ninja are over.

1314
01:11:04,370 --> 01:11:05,370
195...

1315
01:11:13,050 --> 01:11:14,050
196...

1316
01:11:18,710 --> 01:11:19,710
197...

1317
01:11:22,430 --> 01:11:23,430
198...

1318
01:11:26,190 --> 01:11:28,030
Do not count me out!

1319
01:11:28,190 --> 01:11:30,330
I am not through yet!

1320
01:11:33,790 --> 01:11:34,710
You're right.

1321
01:11:34,790 --> 01:11:37,670
All the effort is pointless, if you don't
believe in yourself.

1322
01:11:52,690 --> 01:11:54,090
199...

1323
01:11:55,890 --> 01:11:58,291
199... 199...

1324
01:12:00,210 --> 01:12:04,010
Just one more... one more!

1325
01:12:07,410 --> 01:12:08,890
Just one more.

1326
01:12:12,290 --> 01:12:20,290
A little pause... and we are back.

1327
01:13:04,860 --> 01:13:05,860
He's here!

1328
01:13:13,500 --> 01:13:16,040
Today's history class will be outside.

1329
01:13:17,035 --> 01:13:22,000
As you're all aware, on this rock face are
the sculptures of the Hokages.

1330
01:13:22,360 --> 01:13:23,780
They're in order from the left.

1331
01:13:23,920 --> 01:13:29,360
There's the first, the second,
the third, and the fourth.

1332
01:13:29,800 --> 01:13:31,900
You probably could have figured that out.

1333
01:13:33,560 --> 01:13:36,760
The old man sure looks different up there
than he does now.

1334
01:13:37,280 --> 01:13:38,620
I mean, he used to have hair!

1335
01:13:39,500 --> 01:13:42,460
Iruka-sensei, so who's the fifth Hokage?

1336
01:13:42,840 --> 01:13:43,160
Hmm?

1337
01:13:43,800 --> 01:13:44,800
Hmm.

1338
01:13:44,940 --> 01:13:46,800
That hasn't been decided yet.

1339
01:13:47,300 --> 01:13:49,340
Maybe it'll be your favorite teacher!

1340
01:13:51,180 --> 01:13:52,180
Hmm.

1341
01:13:52,300 --> 01:13:57,660
So, working in an occasional joke to make
for an engaging history lesson, eh, Iruka?

1342
01:13:57,920 --> 01:13:59,000
Oh, Lord Hokage!

1343
01:13:59,300 --> 01:13:59,360
Whoa!

1344
01:13:59,560 --> 01:14:00,560
It's the third!

1345
01:14:00,980 --> 01:14:01,580
Hey, old man!

1346
01:14:01,800 --> 01:14:03,080
What are you doing here?

1347
01:14:03,320 --> 01:14:07,100
I just wanted to look at the mountainside
images like you students are doing.

1348
01:14:07,280 --> 01:14:08,880
Well, you've come at a great time!

1349
01:14:09,080 --> 01:14:10,340
Would you care to join me?

1350
01:14:14,820 --> 01:14:17,930
This is the man whose likeness is carved
up there on that mountain!

1351
01:14:18,510 --> 01:14:19,870
He's the great third Hokage!

1352
01:14:20,830 --> 01:14:22,050
Ah, just look at you.

1353
01:14:22,150 --> 01:14:24,030
You're all so young, unlike me.

1354
01:14:24,860 --> 01:14:28,510
There might be someone among you who will
take the name of Hokage.

1355
01:14:29,790 --> 01:14:33,750
Remember, you have just one life,
so don't choose a road that's impossible.

1356
01:14:34,585 --> 01:14:37,430
It doesn't matter what you do if you live
and die as you like.

1357
01:14:45,055 --> 01:14:47,909
No matter what route you
end up taking, remember

1358
01:14:47,910 --> 01:14:50,721
to protect the people
that are precious to you.

1359
01:14:50,990 --> 01:14:52,640
The people precious to us?

1360
01:14:53,600 --> 01:14:54,360
That's correct.

1361
01:14:54,420 --> 01:14:56,540
The ones you appreciate the very most.

1362
01:14:56,660 --> 01:14:58,820
And trust and love with all your heart.

1363
01:14:58,940 --> 01:15:01,120
Do you have people like that in your life?

1364
01:15:02,040 --> 01:15:04,180
Yeah, I do.

1365
01:15:04,220 --> 01:15:05,300
My dad and my mom.

1366
01:15:05,420 --> 01:15:08,260
And my big brother, even though I don't
like him much.

1367
01:15:08,480 --> 01:15:10,940
Oh yeah, and my dog Gunta.

1368
01:15:10,941 --> 01:15:12,220
I have some too.

1369
01:15:12,400 --> 01:15:13,400
My friends.

1370
01:15:13,960 --> 01:15:14,960
Me too.

1371
01:15:17,500 --> 01:15:20,640
So, do you have people like that too?

1372
01:15:21,280 --> 01:15:22,680
Yes, I do.

1373
01:15:22,800 --> 01:15:23,800
Of course.

1374
01:15:23,940 --> 01:15:24,400
Really?

1375
01:15:24,560 --> 01:15:24,780
Who?

1376
01:15:25,120 --> 01:15:25,500
Who?

1377
01:15:26,100 --> 01:15:29,860
Well, I have my grandson, Konohamaru.

1378
01:15:33,740 --> 01:15:38,060
And I also have all the people in this
village.

1379
01:15:50,920 --> 01:15:51,440
I'm sure you have your own.

1380
01:15:51,441 --> 01:15:54,760
Just as it was for you back then.

1381
01:15:55,880 --> 01:15:58,000
Come on, open your eyes already!

1382
01:16:02,750 --> 01:16:04,360
Hey, what was that for?

1383
01:16:04,675 --> 01:16:05,675
Oh, that?

1384
01:16:06,090 --> 01:16:08,040
To knock sense into you since you have
none.

1385
01:16:08,350 --> 01:16:09,120
I don't!

1386
01:16:09,220 --> 01:16:10,220
Look at you!

1387
01:16:10,260 --> 01:16:13,340
You've been training for three weeks and
you're still at this level?

1388
01:16:13,341 --> 01:16:15,660
If you continue like this, it's pointless.

1389
01:16:16,020 --> 01:16:17,140
Hey, that's not true!

1390
01:16:17,260 --> 01:16:17,920
Give me a break!

1391
01:16:18,100 --> 01:16:19,900
I'm trying as hard as I can here!

1392
01:16:20,160 --> 01:16:21,780
Maybe you are, maybe you're not.

1393
01:16:22,150 --> 01:16:24,717
If you want to succeed
at this summoning jutsu,

1394
01:16:24,718 --> 01:16:27,701
then you must do it like
your life depends on it.

1395
01:16:28,060 --> 01:16:29,600
What do you think I've been doing?

1396
01:16:29,800 --> 01:16:31,620
I train every day like I'm gonna die!

1397
01:16:31,860 --> 01:16:35,120
If you have time to complain about it,
teach me a trick to do it!

1398
01:16:35,540 --> 01:16:36,540
A trick?

1399
01:16:37,305 --> 01:16:38,305
Well, I don't know.

1400
01:16:38,660 --> 01:16:39,100
What?

1401
01:16:39,610 --> 01:16:40,650
You're not gonna teach me?

1402
01:16:41,730 --> 01:16:43,640
You need to put your life at risk.

1403
01:16:44,405 --> 01:16:45,500
My... life?

1404
01:16:45,750 --> 01:16:47,160
That's right, it's no joke.

1405
01:16:47,730 --> 01:16:49,360
Even so, are you willing to do it?

1406
01:16:49,460 --> 01:16:50,000
Of course!

1407
01:16:50,080 --> 01:16:51,200
I always risk my life!

1408
01:16:51,400 --> 01:16:53,720
There's no point in anything if you don't
go all the way!

1409
01:16:54,290 --> 01:16:56,661
I see... Huh?

1410
01:16:57,030 --> 01:16:58,200
Alright, follow me.

1411
01:17:01,660 --> 01:17:02,660
Hey,

1412
01:17:07,890 --> 01:17:10,050
if I do this, can I really summon a frog?

1413
01:17:10,330 --> 01:17:10,870
You bet!

1414
01:17:11,030 --> 01:17:11,570
Of course!

1415
01:17:11,690 --> 01:17:12,150
Absolutely!

1416
01:17:12,390 --> 01:17:13,390
Without a doubt!

1417
01:17:13,805 --> 01:17:14,805
Are you sure?

1418
01:17:15,175 --> 01:17:17,390
Is there anything else you've always
wanted to do?

1419
01:17:17,670 --> 01:17:18,670
Huh?

1420
01:17:19,110 --> 01:17:20,110
Anything?

1421
01:17:20,250 --> 01:17:20,770
What?

1422
01:17:20,830 --> 01:17:22,531
What are you... Gah!

1423
01:17:30,750 --> 01:17:34,190
To tap into his enormous chakra and use
it.

1424
01:17:34,230 --> 01:17:37,870
I'm certain that it's extremely difficult
to control that kind of power.

1425
01:17:38,410 --> 01:17:41,254
It's also true that
Naruto's body is too small a

1426
01:17:41,255 --> 01:17:44,331
vessel to contain the
nine-tailed fox's chakra.

1427
01:17:44,990 --> 01:17:47,962
It's likely that because
that chakra puts such a

1428
01:17:47,963 --> 01:17:50,790
burden on it, Naruto's
body normally suppresses it.

1429
01:17:52,690 --> 01:17:57,330
If the key to drawing out the nine-tailed
fox's chakra is danger and emotion,

1430
01:17:57,670 --> 01:17:59,571
he has to physically
experience them until

1431
01:17:59,572 --> 01:18:03,051
he can learn to summon
the chakra on his own.

1432
01:18:03,250 --> 01:18:06,910
Please forgive me for what I am about to
do, Fourth Okage.

1433
01:18:08,830 --> 01:18:09,830
...

1434
01:18:10,010 --> 01:18:11,010
...

1435
01:18:18,880 --> 01:18:19,880
Where... where are we?

1436
01:18:20,160 --> 01:18:21,160
Tell me...

1437
01:18:21,325 --> 01:18:22,350
Stand up!

1438
01:18:23,850 --> 01:18:24,410
What?

1439
01:18:24,411 --> 01:18:25,510
What's going on?

1440
01:18:26,140 --> 01:18:27,670
Your training ends right here.

1441
01:18:27,970 --> 01:18:28,130
Huh?

1442
01:18:28,790 --> 01:18:30,130
But I haven't done anything yet!

1443
01:18:30,150 --> 01:18:31,150
Naruto!

1444
01:18:31,360 --> 01:18:33,730
Starting now, you must stare death in the
face.

1445
01:18:34,010 --> 01:18:34,370
Death?

1446
01:18:34,770 --> 01:18:35,550
That's right.

1447
01:18:35,650 --> 01:18:39,210
To stave off the horror of death,
you must release enormous chakra.

1448
01:18:39,211 --> 01:18:44,130
Once you experience that, you'll
understand how to release the red chakra.

1449
01:18:44,870 --> 01:18:47,270
If you don't wish to die, do something
about it.

1450
01:18:47,510 --> 01:18:48,510
Now!

1451
01:18:49,610 --> 01:18:50,610
...

1452
01:18:52,110 --> 01:18:53,110
...

1453
01:18:57,090 --> 01:18:58,490
All right, Naruto.

1454
01:18:58,930 --> 01:19:05,111
Now we shall see if the strength that's
been given to you is a blessing or a curse.

1455
01:19:05,350 --> 01:19:06,350
...

1456
01:19:07,550 --> 01:19:13,380
If I don't grab onto something,
I'll die!

1457
01:19:17,380 --> 01:19:18,380
Now!

1458
01:19:22,560 --> 01:19:24,940
It is impossible, Naruto.

1459
01:19:25,200 --> 01:19:26,960
You have to recognize that.

1460
01:19:27,160 --> 01:19:32,280
The rocks are too slippery, and falling at
that speed with the limited control of

1461
01:19:32,281 --> 01:19:35,940
chakra that you possess, you can't
possibly cling to the rock.

1462
01:19:36,620 --> 01:19:38,100
Naruto, you must see it.

1463
01:19:38,200 --> 01:19:41,440
You can only depend on the chakra of the
Nine-Tailed Fox now.

1464
01:19:42,540 --> 01:19:46,460
This time, you have to turn the key
yourself.

1465
01:19:48,780 --> 01:19:52,580
If I go on like this, I really am gonna
die!

1466
01:19:53,760 --> 01:19:54,760
Die!

1467
01:19:59,020 --> 01:19:59,580
What?

1468
01:19:59,581 --> 01:20:00,581
Huh?

1469
01:20:15,890 --> 01:20:16,890
Huh?

1470
01:20:38,860 --> 01:20:42,690
This feeling... it's the red chakra again!

1471
01:20:54,100 --> 01:21:03,740
What is this?

1472
01:21:09,780 --> 01:21:17,160
What is this?

1473
01:21:17,340 --> 01:21:18,600
It's huge!

1474
01:21:18,601 --> 01:21:23,120
Come closer, little boy.

1475
01:21:27,400 --> 01:21:30,640
Um... How wonderful.

1476
01:21:33,040 --> 01:21:35,800
But this accursal gate confines me.

1477
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:38,740
It's that infuriating sealing spell.

1478
01:21:39,280 --> 01:21:41,940
You're... you're the...

1479
01:21:44,100 --> 01:21:45,940
Nine-Tailed Fox!

1480
01:21:48,200 --> 01:21:49,280
Of course!

1481
01:21:50,260 --> 01:21:53,060
The red chakra is this guy's chakra!

1482
01:21:53,360 --> 01:21:55,660
Why are you here, foolish boy?

1483
01:21:55,860 --> 01:21:56,940
What do you want?

1484
01:21:57,200 --> 01:22:02,980
Or have you simply come to offer yourself
to me, so I might feast upon you narrowly?

1485
01:22:06,780 --> 01:22:08,800
Alright, look, you stupid fox!

1486
01:22:09,560 --> 01:22:11,800
You're in my body, and you owe me rent!

1487
01:22:12,100 --> 01:22:14,080
So for payment, I'll take your chakra!

1488
01:22:14,460 --> 01:22:15,540
You got that?

1489
01:22:21,620 --> 01:22:24,460
Well, I suppose I can't kill you,
can I?

1490
01:22:24,680 --> 01:22:27,200
After all, if you die, I die.

1491
01:22:27,580 --> 01:22:30,340
You're Grinch's most impressive little
boy.

1492
01:22:33,720 --> 01:22:34,920
Very well.

1493
01:22:35,200 --> 01:22:39,640
As a reward for making it this far,
I will loan you my chakra.

1494
01:22:40,440 --> 01:22:41,440
Huh?

1495
01:22:46,220 --> 01:22:47,320
This is it!

1496
01:22:49,300 --> 01:22:50,300
Aaaaaaaaaaah!

1497
01:22:51,120 --> 01:22:52,800
Somebody just knew!

1498
01:23:03,440 --> 01:23:05,300
Well done, kid.

1499
01:23:07,080 --> 01:23:08,080
What's this?

1500
01:23:08,600 --> 01:23:10,620
Where in the world am I?

1501
01:23:11,380 --> 01:23:12,380
Aaaaaaaaaaaah!

1502
01:23:14,040 --> 01:23:15,580
That was close.

1503
01:23:15,800 --> 01:23:16,980
Glad I got saved.

1504
01:23:17,300 --> 01:23:20,460
Course I could have done without the
falling on my neck part.

1505
01:23:21,200 --> 01:23:22,240
Look at that!

1506
01:23:23,520 --> 01:23:24,120
Awesome!

1507
01:23:24,320 --> 01:23:26,180
Man, that is humongous!

1508
01:23:27,280 --> 01:23:29,080
Wait, hold on here.

1509
01:23:38,360 --> 01:23:39,360
What's that?

1510
01:23:42,140 --> 01:23:46,440
This is... a toad, isn't it?

1511
01:23:54,620 --> 01:23:56,720
Let's see here...

1512
01:23:58,100 --> 01:23:59,660
There's no tail there!

1513
01:24:02,700 --> 01:24:03,920
I did it!

1514
01:24:04,140 --> 01:24:07,740
I didn't summon this... or this!

1515
01:24:07,940 --> 01:24:11,940
It's really... a real... toad!

1516
01:24:14,770 --> 01:24:19,760
Looks like he released the Chakra of the
Nine-Tailed Fox all on his own this time.

1517
01:24:21,470 --> 01:24:24,720
But still, I certainly can't say that he's
proficient at it yet.

1518
01:24:25,350 --> 01:24:30,840
He overdid it with the Chakra's power...
to have summoned him of all things.

1519
01:24:32,140 --> 01:24:33,760
You little snot!

1520
01:24:34,060 --> 01:24:37,360
Just whose head do you think you're
dancing around on top of anyway?

1521
01:24:37,361 --> 01:24:43,000
Well, let me tell you, I am the wise and
powerful Lord Gamabunta, the Chief Toad!

1522
01:24:43,001 --> 01:24:44,001
And you're an idiot!

1523
01:24:44,500 --> 01:24:45,720
Now shut up!

1524
01:24:46,980 --> 01:24:47,980
Ah!

1525
01:24:48,580 --> 01:24:49,580
Ah!

1526
01:24:51,380 --> 01:24:51,980
Ah!

1527
01:24:52,180 --> 01:24:52,500
Ah!

1528
01:24:52,840 --> 01:24:53,220
Ah!

1529
01:24:53,221 --> 01:24:54,221
Ah!

1530
01:24:56,220 --> 01:24:57,760
What is this guy?

1531
01:24:57,820 --> 01:25:00,480
He seemed cool, but... give me a break
here!

1532
01:25:00,720 --> 01:25:01,720
Ah!

1533
01:25:01,900 --> 01:25:05,600
Just when I finally get to breathe some
fresh air again...

1534
01:25:05,601 --> 01:25:08,480
I find some weird kid tap-dancing on my
head!

1535
01:25:09,160 --> 01:25:10,200
Hey, Jiraiya!

1536
01:25:10,500 --> 01:25:12,480
Where are you, Jiraiya?

1537
01:25:12,740 --> 01:25:14,700
Just what do you think you're doing?

1538
01:25:15,400 --> 01:25:16,400
Whoa!

1539
01:25:18,520 --> 01:25:23,600
Well, this doesn't look good... Even
I'm not able to handle Gamabunta.

1540
01:25:23,780 --> 01:25:25,100
I mean, he's a real handful.

1541
01:25:26,680 --> 01:25:27,200
Jiraiya!

1542
01:25:27,201 --> 01:25:28,900
Show yourself, you baboon!

1543
01:25:30,180 --> 01:25:30,700
Hmm...

1544
01:25:30,701 --> 01:25:33,519
It would be a pain in
the neck if he found me

1545
01:25:33,519 --> 01:25:35,580
out, so I'd better
hightail it out of here.

1546
01:25:36,520 --> 01:25:38,680
Hey, little snot!

1547
01:25:39,420 --> 01:25:40,080
Uh, yeah?

1548
01:25:40,340 --> 01:25:42,400
Where's Jiraiya hiding?

1549
01:25:42,820 --> 01:25:43,120
Huh?

1550
01:25:43,660 --> 01:25:44,960
Who's this Jiraiya?

1551
01:25:45,060 --> 01:25:47,021
I don't know any...
Don't play dumb!

1552
01:25:47,320 --> 01:25:50,480
I'm talking about that lecher who calls
himself the Toad Sage!

1553
01:25:50,820 --> 01:25:52,140
Now where is he?

1554
01:25:53,500 --> 01:25:54,500
Well...

1555
01:25:55,160 --> 01:25:56,860
Man, he's scary!

1556
01:25:57,440 --> 01:26:00,264
Look, I'm giving you an
order, and if you can follow

1557
01:26:00,265 --> 01:26:02,840
it, I'll even consider
making you my henchman!

1558
01:26:03,240 --> 01:26:04,900
Now hurry up and answer me!

1559
01:26:05,560 --> 01:26:06,760
Okay, okay!

1560
01:26:06,920 --> 01:26:11,100
If you're talking about the Pervy Sage,
he's on the cliff up there, Chief Toad!

1561
01:26:11,320 --> 01:26:12,320
Up there?

1562
01:26:12,740 --> 01:26:16,320
Um, can I ask you one question,
Sir Toad, sir?

1563
01:26:16,600 --> 01:26:17,640
What is it?

1564
01:26:18,080 --> 01:26:20,860
What business do you have with that Pervy
Sage, anyway?

1565
01:26:21,580 --> 01:26:24,940
That's the very same question I want to
ask that pervert!

1566
01:26:25,200 --> 01:26:27,932
I mean, what in the
world does that fool want

1567
01:26:27,933 --> 01:26:30,720
with me, summoning me
to a dank place like this?

1568
01:26:31,100 --> 01:26:33,981
Oh, but, um... What now?

1569
01:26:34,820 --> 01:26:38,280
Well, actually, the funny thing is that
I'm the one who summoned you.

1570
01:26:38,400 --> 01:26:42,210
You see, I fell off the cliff, and I
thought that maybe you could rescue me, so.

1571
01:26:42,211 --> 01:26:42,660
..

1572
01:26:42,661 --> 01:26:43,720
Thanks, boss!

1573
01:26:50,740 --> 01:26:53,555
There's no way a little
squirt like you could

1574
01:26:53,556 --> 01:26:56,621
have enough power to
summon up a being like me!

1575
01:26:56,940 --> 01:26:57,080
Huh?

1576
01:26:57,560 --> 01:26:59,240
No, no, it's true, it's true!

1577
01:26:59,320 --> 01:27:01,680
I mean, I really, truly summoned you!

1578
01:27:01,681 --> 01:27:06,000
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1579
01:27:10,680 --> 01:27:12,700
Knock it off, you Toad jerk!

1580
01:27:13,240 --> 01:27:17,100
You've been talking down to me and saying
whatever you want since you first got here!

1581
01:27:17,340 --> 01:27:20,140
But I'm the one who summoned you,
and that means I'm your master!

1582
01:27:20,280 --> 01:27:22,760
You have to start respecting me and doing
what I say!

1583
01:27:22,860 --> 01:27:23,920
You got that, Toad?

1584
01:27:25,500 --> 01:27:25,960
Hmm?

1585
01:27:25,961 --> 01:27:26,961
What was that?

1586
01:27:27,160 --> 01:27:28,460
You've got some nerve!

1587
01:27:28,580 --> 01:27:30,120
Who do you think you're talking to?

1588
01:27:30,121 --> 01:27:30,380
You!

1589
01:27:30,400 --> 01:27:32,920
A meaningless little squirt like you!

1590
01:27:33,340 --> 01:27:38,820
Barely old enough to stand, and you dare
to say to Lord Gamabunta, the Chief Toad,

1591
01:27:38,940 --> 01:27:40,300
that you're his master?

1592
01:27:40,400 --> 01:27:41,400
That's it!

1593
01:27:41,720 --> 01:27:45,840
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1594
01:27:47,760 --> 01:27:50,320
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1595
01:28:02,540 --> 01:28:03,720
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1596
01:28:12,840 --> 01:28:16,480
Well, it looks like he reached the top
thanks to Gamabunta.

1597
01:28:16,890 --> 01:28:18,780
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1598
01:28:20,480 --> 01:28:21,480
Whoa!

1599
01:28:22,780 --> 01:28:24,840
That was awesome!

1600
01:28:26,220 --> 01:28:27,680
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1601
01:28:29,200 --> 01:28:31,880
I hate to tell you this, you little snot!

1602
01:28:31,881 --> 01:28:36,240
But even if I were willing to believe that
you were actually the one who summoned

1603
01:28:36,241 --> 01:28:39,340
me... And trust me, kid,
that's a really, really big if.

1604
01:28:39,460 --> 01:28:42,305
If you're the kind of guy
who could fall off my back that

1605
01:28:42,306 --> 01:28:45,840
easily, then there's no way I
could ever accept you as my master!

1606
01:28:46,040 --> 01:28:46,600
You got it?

1607
01:28:47,000 --> 01:28:47,240
Hmm?

1608
01:28:47,880 --> 01:28:48,880
Hmm?

1609
01:28:50,740 --> 01:28:55,920
Now, since I'm back in the world,
after such a very, very long time...

1610
01:28:55,921 --> 01:28:58,920
If Jiraiya doesn't need me, I'm going for
a walk!

1611
01:28:59,100 --> 01:28:59,440
No!

1612
01:28:59,800 --> 01:29:00,800
Wait!

1613
01:29:01,080 --> 01:29:03,920
Listen, why don't you just get out of here
and go home?

1614
01:29:04,260 --> 01:29:08,040
Because it's clear you're incapable of
serving as my henchman!

1615
01:29:08,700 --> 01:29:09,700
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1616
01:29:09,960 --> 01:29:11,440
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1617
01:29:15,740 --> 01:29:16,740
What?

1618
01:29:27,670 --> 01:29:29,450
What do you suppose you're doing now?

1619
01:29:29,990 --> 01:29:34,730
Fine, if making you respect me depends on
me staying on your back, well then...

1620
01:29:34,731 --> 01:29:37,010
I'll just make sure I don't get off your
back!

1621
01:29:37,030 --> 01:29:39,250
I'll keep your back the rest of the day no
matter what!

1622
01:29:39,650 --> 01:29:40,650
What?

1623
01:29:40,810 --> 01:29:43,420
That's right, and when
I do, then you'll have no

1624
01:29:43,421 --> 01:29:46,490
choice but to recognize me
as your undisputed master!

1625
01:29:46,930 --> 01:29:48,910
You really are a snot!

1626
01:29:49,110 --> 01:29:52,430
Fine if that's what you want, but don't
think I'm going to go easy on you!

1627
01:29:52,431 --> 01:29:53,431
You!

1628
01:30:01,450 --> 01:30:03,470
I must grip with chakra!

1629
01:30:05,010 --> 01:30:06,890
I don't have enough chakra!

1630
01:30:07,510 --> 01:30:09,310
Listen carefully, cheap-toed!

1631
01:30:09,530 --> 01:30:11,550
My name is Naruko Uzumaki!

1632
01:30:12,310 --> 01:30:14,350
I'm going to become Okage someday!

1633
01:30:14,590 --> 01:30:15,610
Don't forget that!

1634
01:30:17,930 --> 01:30:19,450
I don't care!

1635
01:30:27,790 --> 01:30:28,390
Welcome!

1636
01:30:28,670 --> 01:30:29,270
Come on in!

1637
01:30:29,610 --> 01:30:32,450
I am going to eat till I can't eat no
more!

1638
01:30:33,010 --> 01:30:35,670
Those guys are eating barbecue again.

1639
01:30:35,830 --> 01:30:39,190
Giving themselves a reward for training so
hard, I guess.

1640
01:30:39,745 --> 01:30:43,590
Hey, I thought you were told not to let
Gaara out of your sight, Konkuro.

1641
01:30:44,440 --> 01:30:45,440
Oh, don't worry.

1642
01:30:45,680 --> 01:30:50,110
Even someone like him wouldn't dare to do
anything in broad daylight.

1643
01:30:50,990 --> 01:30:52,290
But about you.

1644
01:30:52,770 --> 01:30:54,350
That guy Shikamaru would have...

1645
01:30:54,370 --> 01:30:56,890
Whatever his name is, he's the first guy
you're fighting, right?

1646
01:30:57,510 --> 01:30:59,530
Shouldn't you be formulating a battle
plan?

1647
01:31:00,990 --> 01:31:03,790
There's no way that I would lose to a guy
who's at that level.

1648
01:31:04,110 --> 01:31:05,110
No way.

1649
01:31:05,380 --> 01:31:06,610
You blew it, didn't you?

1650
01:31:06,830 --> 01:31:07,830
What?

1651
01:31:07,940 --> 01:31:10,625
If you had taken the
exam one year earlier, then

1652
01:31:10,626 --> 01:31:13,310
you would have made
Chunin easily, right, Tamari?

1653
01:31:14,770 --> 01:31:15,770
Don't say that.

1654
01:31:20,330 --> 01:31:21,330
What?

1655
01:31:21,820 --> 01:31:22,820
What did you just say?

1656
01:31:23,740 --> 01:31:27,690
I'm going to have you three ninja,
the best from the Hidden Sand Village,

1657
01:31:27,890 --> 01:31:29,930
participate in the upcoming Chunin exam.

1658
01:31:30,510 --> 01:31:34,190
But the reason that I'm having you do so
is not for you to pass the Chunin exam.

1659
01:31:35,280 --> 01:31:39,930
We must use this chance, so that we're
able to crush the Hidden Leaf Village.

1660
01:31:40,330 --> 01:31:41,330
But why?

1661
01:31:41,800 --> 01:31:43,360
Why are we turning on the Leaf Village?

1662
01:31:43,970 --> 01:31:46,030
Didn't we sign the Treaty of Alliance with
them?

1663
01:31:46,730 --> 01:31:47,830
Yes, we did.

1664
01:31:48,730 --> 01:31:50,510
And that treaty is the whole problem.

1665
01:31:50,511 --> 01:31:52,350
I don't get it.

1666
01:31:52,370 --> 01:31:53,370
What do you mean?

1667
01:31:54,020 --> 01:31:56,390
You Genin aren't aware of all the details
of this.

1668
01:31:56,590 --> 01:32:00,990
But when the Treaty of Alliance was
signed, that idiot feudal lord who rules

1669
01:32:00,991 --> 01:32:05,430
us used it as an opportunity to force
military cutbacks on our village.

1670
01:32:06,730 --> 01:32:08,970
He also delegated to
the Hidden Leaf Village

1671
01:32:08,971 --> 01:32:11,591
matters that should
have been handled by us.

1672
01:32:11,870 --> 01:32:15,049
And even worse, he
significantly cut our village's

1673
01:32:15,050 --> 01:32:17,510
budget and slashed
the number of shinobi.

1674
01:32:17,511 --> 01:32:22,050
When the head of our country is weak,
we, the country's arms and legs, suffer.

1675
01:32:22,250 --> 01:32:24,610
And so we took the only choice left to us.

1676
01:32:24,770 --> 01:32:28,430
Improve the quality of every shinobi to
maintain our military strength.

1677
01:32:29,410 --> 01:32:33,630
That's why shinobi like you were created.

1678
01:32:34,890 --> 01:32:35,890
Gaara.

1679
01:32:36,630 --> 01:32:39,750
The Land of Wind's very existence is in
danger.

1680
01:32:39,890 --> 01:32:42,170
More danger than it's ever been in before.

1681
01:32:42,930 --> 01:32:47,290
But still, that idiot feudal lord and all
his incompetent advisors...

1682
01:32:47,510 --> 01:32:49,270
are too blind to see it.

1683
01:32:50,050 --> 01:32:55,526
So the Kazekage who detected this
weakening of the might of the Sand Village.

1684
01:32:55,527 --> 01:32:55,530
..

1685
01:32:55,531 --> 01:33:00,530
joined hands with the Sound Village to
show our feudal lord his stupidity.

1686
01:33:00,870 --> 01:33:05,950
By crushing the Hidden Leaf Village and
restoring our own, this needs to be done

1687
01:33:05,951 --> 01:33:09,370
to make that idiot aware of the importance
of preparing for a crisis.

1688
01:33:12,730 --> 01:33:15,031
If any more time
passes, our Sand Village

1689
01:33:15,032 --> 01:33:18,151
will be completely
drained of its abilities.

1690
01:33:19,130 --> 01:33:21,730
This is our only chance.

1691
01:33:22,130 --> 01:33:27,310
Now Gaara, this mission depends entirely
upon your skills.

1692
01:33:30,200 --> 01:33:31,200
Yes.

1693
01:33:31,350 --> 01:33:33,950
This is an A-plus ranked mission.

1694
01:33:34,210 --> 01:33:36,050
Make sure you succeed.

1695
01:33:36,430 --> 01:33:37,430
Okay.

1696
01:33:38,530 --> 01:33:39,530
Yes.

1697
01:33:43,490 --> 01:33:44,530
I'm bored.

1698
01:33:44,710 --> 01:33:47,470
The day sure goes by slowly when you're
not doing anything.

1699
01:33:47,490 --> 01:33:48,490
Not even much anything.

1700
01:33:49,310 --> 01:33:50,310
I guess.

1701
01:33:56,350 --> 01:33:58,650
Good work, Baki.

1702
01:34:00,070 --> 01:34:01,970
Thank you, Lord Kazekage.

1703
01:34:02,290 --> 01:34:06,430
I successfully moved all three ponds to
the final rounds as planned.

1704
01:34:07,290 --> 01:34:08,290
Hm.

1705
01:34:08,750 --> 01:34:11,990
And the pact with the Sound Village has
progressed as well?

1706
01:34:12,150 --> 01:34:13,150
Yes sir.

1707
01:34:14,930 --> 01:34:15,930
Hm.

1708
01:34:16,610 --> 01:34:19,230
Contains the details of the Sound
Village's plan.

1709
01:34:34,610 --> 01:34:36,410
Is there something else?

1710
01:34:37,390 --> 01:34:38,370
Well... What?

1711
01:34:38,770 --> 01:34:39,770
Out with it.

1712
01:34:40,010 --> 01:34:40,870
Yes, sir.

1713
01:34:41,030 --> 01:34:43,929
I was wondering if you
could position soldiers near

1714
01:34:43,930 --> 01:34:46,610
the border under the
pretext of a tactical exercise.

1715
01:34:47,130 --> 01:34:48,770
With just the four of us...

1716
01:34:48,771 --> 01:34:50,775
The Hidden Leaf Village
isn't full of Dimwits,

1717
01:34:50,776 --> 01:34:53,451
and the Anvu Black Ops
are active in that area.

1718
01:34:53,610 --> 01:34:56,670
If we do what you ask, they'll see right
through what we're planning.

1719
01:34:56,950 --> 01:34:58,850
Everything we work toward will be ruined.

1720
01:35:00,410 --> 01:35:03,750
But with only our current military
capability...

1721
01:35:03,751 --> 01:35:05,590
That's why I've sent Gaara and the others.

1722
01:35:06,110 --> 01:35:09,310
The restoration of Sound Village's glory
is in your hands.

1723
01:35:10,570 --> 01:35:11,570
Now... go.

1724
01:35:12,730 --> 01:35:13,730
Yes, sir.

1725
01:35:15,210 --> 01:35:16,210
Yes, sir.

1726
01:35:21,160 --> 01:35:23,320
How do you like that, Chief Toad?

1727
01:35:23,480 --> 01:35:25,140
I'm still on your back!

1728
01:35:26,820 --> 01:35:27,380
That's right!

1729
01:35:27,580 --> 01:35:28,700
I beat you!

1730
01:35:29,660 --> 01:35:30,660
No!

1731
01:35:36,820 --> 01:35:38,460
If he falls like that, he'll die!

1732
01:35:49,180 --> 01:35:51,480
Too bad for you, little snot.

1733
01:35:51,800 --> 01:35:54,140
And you almost made it, too.

1734
01:35:58,560 --> 01:35:58,860
Amazing.

1735
01:35:59,200 --> 01:36:03,200
He could hold out so long against a tough
opponent like Gamabunta.

1736
01:36:17,450 --> 01:36:19,110
Naruto Uzumaki, huh?

1737
01:36:19,390 --> 01:36:21,410
You scoundrel, Jiraiya.

1738
01:36:21,570 --> 01:36:25,630
I am fully aware that this boy summoned me
all on his own.

1739
01:36:25,631 --> 01:36:27,050
He is courageous.

1740
01:36:27,750 --> 01:36:32,670
It's the first time since the fourth Hokage
that someone has dared to climb on my head.

1741
01:36:32,950 --> 01:36:37,670
As may be expected after that battle,
he looks completely drained of energy.

1742
01:36:38,010 --> 01:36:41,496
I don't mind giving him
some of my power, but I believe

1743
01:36:41,497 --> 01:36:44,930
that taking him to a place
of healing would be best.

1744
01:36:48,130 --> 01:36:49,630
What was that?

1745
01:37:02,320 --> 01:37:03,320
Huh?

1746
01:37:06,060 --> 01:37:08,460
So... you decided to wake up, huh?

1747
01:37:09,720 --> 01:37:10,720
Where am I?

1748
01:37:10,980 --> 01:37:11,980
What is this?

1749
01:37:12,200 --> 01:37:13,200
The hospital.

1750
01:37:13,430 --> 01:37:15,990
They said you've been out cold like this
for three days straight.

1751
01:37:17,200 --> 01:37:18,200
Three days?

1752
01:37:20,535 --> 01:37:22,945
I went to all the trouble
of getting this stuff for

1753
01:37:22,946 --> 01:37:25,540
Choji, and then the doctors
told me he couldn't have it.

1754
01:37:25,830 --> 01:37:26,830
Such a drag.

1755
01:37:27,360 --> 01:37:28,760
But at least we can eat it.

1756
01:37:29,260 --> 01:37:29,780
Choji?

1757
01:37:29,781 --> 01:37:32,100
You mean he's here in the hospital too?

1758
01:37:32,750 --> 01:37:33,920
Nothing to worry about.

1759
01:37:34,640 --> 01:37:36,740
All he's got is a bad case of indigestion.

1760
01:37:37,500 --> 01:37:39,200
He ate one short rib too many.

1761
01:37:40,180 --> 01:37:41,520
I should have figured.

1762
01:37:41,620 --> 01:37:42,640
That's just like him.

1763
01:37:42,780 --> 01:37:43,060
Yeah.

1764
01:37:43,320 --> 01:37:46,620
Well, you two are just lucky I'm around,
or you wouldn't have any visitors.

1765
01:37:47,060 --> 01:37:48,060
Here.

1766
01:37:48,680 --> 01:37:49,460
Oh, wow.

1767
01:37:49,560 --> 01:37:50,560
This looks delicious.

1768
01:37:53,200 --> 01:37:53,680
What?

1769
01:37:53,990 --> 01:37:54,990
What is it now?

1770
01:37:56,625 --> 01:37:58,080
Let's eat it in front of Choji.

1771
01:37:58,160 --> 01:37:59,220
It'll drive him crazy.

1772
01:37:59,221 --> 01:38:00,700
Man, that's mean.

1773
01:38:01,640 --> 01:38:02,640
I like it.

1774
01:38:29,530 --> 01:38:31,370
Why save him?

1775
01:38:31,930 --> 01:38:34,470
Because he's... he's my student.

1776
01:38:34,770 --> 01:38:37,230
And also because he is precious to me.

1777
01:38:38,650 --> 01:38:39,650
Oh, I see!

1778
01:38:46,340 --> 01:38:47,340
What am I?

1779
01:39:05,820 --> 01:39:07,110
I'm still starving!

1780
01:39:20,850 --> 01:39:22,160
Come on!

1781
01:39:22,710 --> 01:39:24,440
Don't torture me like that, Shikamaru!

1782
01:39:28,260 --> 01:39:32,000
I can't move... my body...

1783
01:39:35,320 --> 01:39:39,440
What the heck do you think you're doing in
here, you rat?!

1784
01:39:39,441 --> 01:39:42,280
Hey man, go easy!

1785
01:39:42,660 --> 01:39:44,971
I'm using my shadow
possession jutsu, so when

1786
01:39:44,972 --> 01:39:47,260
you're bashing him,
you're bashing me too.

1787
01:39:47,580 --> 01:39:48,400
You got it?

1788
01:39:48,600 --> 01:39:50,000
Oh, sorry, Shikamaru!

1789
01:39:56,840 --> 01:39:58,230
Hey Choji, feeling better?

1790
01:39:59,280 --> 01:40:00,280
Oh, Ino!

1791
01:40:03,490 --> 01:40:04,490
Alright!

1792
01:40:04,570 --> 01:40:06,030
A pretty girl with food!

1793
01:40:06,250 --> 01:40:07,510
This is my lucky day!

1794
01:40:13,670 --> 01:40:14,190
Well?

1795
01:40:14,450 --> 01:40:16,850
Are you gonna tell us what you were gonna
do?!

1796
01:40:16,851 --> 01:40:18,710
I was going to kill him.

1797
01:40:18,970 --> 01:40:19,970
What?

1798
01:40:20,250 --> 01:40:22,150
This guy's one cool customer.

1799
01:40:22,490 --> 01:40:23,290
Look at him.

1800
01:40:23,390 --> 01:40:26,210
He's not even phased by my shadow
possession jutsu.

1801
01:40:28,470 --> 01:40:30,890
You already beat him once in the
competition.

1802
01:40:31,570 --> 01:40:32,710
What's your problem?

1803
01:40:32,830 --> 01:40:33,910
Wasn't that enough for you?

1804
01:40:34,230 --> 01:40:37,410
Do you have some kind of personal grudge
against him or something?

1805
01:40:38,290 --> 01:40:39,990
It's nothing that complicated.

1806
01:40:40,090 --> 01:40:42,170
I simply want to kill him, that's all.

1807
01:40:42,171 --> 01:40:43,090
You know what?

1808
01:40:43,091 --> 01:40:44,091
You're sick in the head!

1809
01:40:44,310 --> 01:40:45,310
You're crazy!

1810
01:40:45,370 --> 01:40:45,590
Yeah.

1811
01:40:45,770 --> 01:40:49,070
You think we're gonna just stand by and
let you do whatever you want?

1812
01:40:49,360 --> 01:40:50,690
You sick selfish psycho.

1813
01:40:52,310 --> 01:40:54,330
This guy gives me the creeps.

1814
01:40:54,890 --> 01:40:57,030
There's always been something weird about
him.

1815
01:40:57,370 --> 01:40:58,370
Scary.

1816
01:40:58,410 --> 01:41:03,310
If he decides to make a move, I'm not sure
we'll be able to stop him.

1817
01:41:03,985 --> 01:41:07,630
If you don't stay out of my way,
I'll have to kill you too as well.

1818
01:41:07,950 --> 01:41:08,970
Oh really?!

1819
01:41:08,971 --> 01:41:10,570
Well let's just see you try it!

1820
01:41:10,630 --> 01:41:11,270
Hey, whoa kid!

1821
01:41:11,350 --> 01:41:12,350
Take it easy!

1822
01:41:13,130 --> 01:41:15,970
Best thing to do is try and bluff our way
out of this.

1823
01:41:17,210 --> 01:41:18,110
Yeah, yeah.

1824
01:41:18,210 --> 01:41:20,090
We watched your last match against Lee.

1825
01:41:20,170 --> 01:41:21,170
We know you're tough.

1826
01:41:21,290 --> 01:41:25,830
But you know, Naruto and I have a few
little tricks up our sleeves as well.

1827
01:41:26,270 --> 01:41:28,370
We were holding back during the
competition.

1828
01:41:28,530 --> 01:41:30,230
There are things you haven't seen yet.

1829
01:41:30,770 --> 01:41:33,490
On top of that, hey, it's two against one.

1830
01:41:33,750 --> 01:41:35,470
So don't be a fool, okay?

1831
01:41:35,830 --> 01:41:37,810
Just take my advice and go.

1832
01:41:38,750 --> 01:41:39,230
Quietly.

1833
01:41:39,231 --> 01:41:40,650
I'll say it once more.

1834
01:41:41,070 --> 01:41:44,530
If you get in my way, I'll kill you.

1835
01:41:44,950 --> 01:41:46,330
Okay, plan B.

1836
01:41:47,090 --> 01:41:48,550
And I'll say it again!

1837
01:41:48,650 --> 01:41:49,750
Let's see you try it!

1838
01:41:49,880 --> 01:41:50,770
Back off, will ya?

1839
01:41:50,830 --> 01:41:51,910
We don't want to go there!

1840
01:41:52,655 --> 01:41:55,450
This guy fights like he's mad,
like he's a demon or something.

1841
01:41:56,840 --> 01:41:59,470
He can act like a demon if he wants to,
but you know what?

1842
01:41:59,650 --> 01:42:01,490
I got the real thing inside of me!

1843
01:42:04,730 --> 01:42:05,170
Idiot.

1844
01:42:05,390 --> 01:42:06,390
Leave this to me.

1845
01:42:06,760 --> 01:42:08,200
What's the point of getting him mad?

1846
01:42:10,040 --> 01:42:11,040
A demon, huh?

1847
01:42:13,200 --> 01:42:15,450
My demon is as real as yours is.

1848
01:42:16,765 --> 01:42:21,690
From my birth, my upbringing was not what
most people would consider a happy one.

1849
01:42:21,970 --> 01:42:27,270
To ensure that I became the strongest of
shinobi, my father had cast his ninjutsu

1850
01:42:27,271 --> 01:42:31,150
on me, infusing my unborn self with a sand
spirit.

1851
01:42:31,350 --> 01:42:34,930
I destroyed the life of a woman who gave
birth to me.

1852
01:42:35,290 --> 01:42:37,290
I was born a monster.

1853
01:42:40,830 --> 01:42:42,090
Can it be true?

1854
01:42:43,410 --> 01:42:45,350
He's got one inside of him, too?

1855
01:42:48,570 --> 01:42:51,690
Gee, what a swell guy your dad must have
been.

1856
01:42:51,790 --> 01:42:53,650
He really must have loved you a lot.

1857
01:42:53,990 --> 01:42:55,570
You speak of love?

1858
01:42:56,350 --> 01:42:58,590
Don't measure me by your standards.

1859
01:43:00,590 --> 01:43:01,590
Love?

1860
01:43:02,410 --> 01:43:03,410
Family?

1861
01:43:03,750 --> 01:43:09,911
The only emotional ties I have to my family
are the ones I'd like to wrap around.

1862
01:43:10,030 --> 01:43:11,810
They're only ties of hate.

1863
01:43:13,030 --> 01:43:16,389
Given life by the death of
my mother, I was brought

1864
01:43:16,390 --> 01:43:19,410
into being and nurtured as
the salvation of the village.

1865
01:43:19,940 --> 01:43:21,810
I was the Kazekage child.

1866
01:43:22,590 --> 01:43:26,170
My father taught me the innermost secrets
of the shinobi.

1867
01:43:26,390 --> 01:43:29,610
He pampered and protected me, and left me
to myself.

1868
01:43:30,070 --> 01:43:32,710
For a time, I thought that was love.

1869
01:43:33,030 --> 01:43:37,090
Those who get to be too strong are apt to
become feared.

1870
01:43:37,990 --> 01:43:41,750
The jutsu that gave me birth had
unbalanced something in my mind.

1871
01:43:41,930 --> 01:43:46,770
Even the fools in my village finally
realized I had emotional problems.

1872
01:43:47,350 --> 01:43:52,970
My father, the Kazekage, had created me as
his ultimate weapon, but I eventually

1873
01:43:52,971 --> 01:43:56,110
became a threat to the very village I was
meant to save.

1874
01:43:56,410 --> 01:44:01,030
By the time I was six, I became a figure
of terror to the villagers.

1875
01:44:01,031 --> 01:44:06,030
To them, I was a relic of the past that
they wished would disappear.

1876
01:44:06,970 --> 01:44:11,670
So you see, I had failed at the one
purpose for which I was given life.

1877
01:44:12,870 --> 01:44:15,550
What then was left for me in this
existence?

1878
01:44:15,650 --> 01:44:16,790
Why go on living?

1879
01:44:17,190 --> 01:44:20,390
For a long time, I couldn't find an answer
to that.

1880
01:44:20,950 --> 01:44:23,490
But in order to live, you need a purpose.

1881
01:44:23,790 --> 01:44:25,810
To exist for no reason.

1882
01:44:26,010 --> 01:44:27,670
It's the same as being dead.

1883
01:44:28,750 --> 01:44:31,170
What is this guy talking about?

1884
01:44:33,770 --> 01:44:35,490
I know just what he means.

1885
01:44:36,070 --> 01:44:37,070
Exactly.

1886
01:44:37,610 --> 01:44:40,010
He's... he's the same as me.

1887
01:44:41,490 --> 01:44:43,850
Then in time, the answer came to me.

1888
01:44:44,390 --> 01:44:48,650
To put it simply, my reason for living is
in the killing of others.

1889
01:44:48,870 --> 01:44:52,370
For years, I lived in fear of those who
were sent to murder me.

1890
01:44:52,710 --> 01:44:54,510
But now I am at peace.

1891
01:44:55,490 --> 01:44:58,070
I killed many would-be assassins.

1892
01:44:58,490 --> 01:45:02,150
And it was while I was doing it that the
truth was made clear to me.

1893
01:45:02,810 --> 01:45:04,790
I live solely for myself.

1894
01:45:04,990 --> 01:45:06,550
I love only myself.

1895
01:45:07,390 --> 01:45:11,710
As it was the death of my mother that
first gave me life, now it is the death of

1896
01:45:11,711 --> 01:45:14,910
others that sustains me, that makes me
almost happy to be alive.

1897
01:45:15,870 --> 01:45:17,850
And there's no end to it.

1898
01:45:18,490 --> 01:45:23,690
As long as there are still people to kill
in this great, wide-crowded world.

1899
01:45:24,510 --> 01:45:26,430
I will never disappear.

1900
01:45:28,030 --> 01:45:29,030
This freak!

1901
01:45:29,450 --> 01:45:30,750
He's out of his mind!

1902
01:45:31,450 --> 01:45:32,950
I was alone, too.

1903
01:45:33,610 --> 01:45:36,710
I didn't know what I was here for,
why I was alive.

1904
01:45:37,390 --> 01:45:39,170
Until Iruka-sensei came along.

1905
01:45:39,790 --> 01:45:41,590
He saw what was in me.

1906
01:45:42,110 --> 01:45:44,710
He gave me a purpose, a reason for living.

1907
01:45:45,430 --> 01:45:47,230
But this guy had no one.

1908
01:45:47,830 --> 01:45:49,950
He had to find the answer on his own.

1909
01:45:50,510 --> 01:45:52,730
And this is what he came up with.

1910
01:45:52,731 --> 01:45:54,970
To kill in order to live.

1911
01:45:57,250 --> 01:45:59,710
Could I have ended up like that if...

1912
01:46:04,460 --> 01:46:08,520
We're so different, but we're so close to
being the same.

1913
01:46:10,000 --> 01:46:10,560
No!

1914
01:46:10,920 --> 01:46:13,000
I don't think I can beat this guy!

1915
01:46:19,320 --> 01:46:21,360
He shouldn't be able to do that.

1916
01:46:21,600 --> 01:46:24,160
Not with my Shadow Possession jutsu on
him.

1917
01:46:29,880 --> 01:46:31,040
I don't think I can beat him.

1918
01:46:31,240 --> 01:46:33,420
Hey, wake up!

1919
01:46:33,620 --> 01:46:35,300
Oh man, what a drag!

1920
01:46:35,740 --> 01:46:36,740
Naruto!

1921
01:46:37,200 --> 01:46:39,240
Now, let me feel alive.

1922
01:46:40,220 --> 01:46:41,220
Incoming!

1923
01:46:41,300 --> 01:46:42,520
Alright, that's enough.

1924
01:46:43,940 --> 01:46:45,240
Save it till tomorrow.

1925
01:46:45,400 --> 01:46:47,560
That's when the final competition begins.

1926
01:46:49,340 --> 01:46:50,700
Don't leave me alone.

1927
01:46:52,180 --> 01:46:54,480
I'm not bleeding, but it hurts a lot.

1928
01:46:57,580 --> 01:46:58,740
What am I?

1929
01:46:59,440 --> 01:47:00,740
What am I?

1930
01:47:25,665 --> 01:47:27,640
All the same, I will kill you.

1931
01:47:27,720 --> 01:47:29,220
I'll kill you all.

1932
01:47:29,221 --> 01:47:30,221
Ah...

1933
01:47:33,600 --> 01:47:34,280
Whoa!

1934
01:47:34,620 --> 01:47:34,860
Oh!

1935
01:47:35,300 --> 01:47:35,380
Oh!

1936
01:47:35,720 --> 01:47:36,400
Oh!

1937
01:47:36,600 --> 01:47:36,980
Oh!

1938
01:47:36,981 --> 01:47:37,380
One!

1939
01:47:37,600 --> 01:47:38,600
Two!

1940
01:47:40,750 --> 01:47:41,750
One!

1941
01:47:42,090 --> 01:47:43,750
I love you!

1942
01:47:43,870 --> 01:47:44,130
Three!

1943
01:47:44,330 --> 01:47:47,070
My love for curry is never-ending.

1944
01:47:47,310 --> 01:47:47,590
Four!

1945
01:47:47,690 --> 01:47:48,690
Cheers!

1946
01:47:50,050 --> 01:47:50,550
Hooray!

1947
01:47:50,790 --> 01:47:52,270
All over the world, look!

1948
01:47:52,410 --> 01:47:53,410
We're having fun.

1949
01:47:53,670 --> 01:47:55,090
Let's look up in the sky.

1950
01:47:55,150 --> 01:47:56,430
Let's get up high.

1951
01:47:56,830 --> 01:47:57,850
Oh yeah!

1952
01:47:58,610 --> 01:47:59,670
Oh yeah!

1953
01:48:19,830 --> 01:48:27,830
A little pause... and we are back.

1954
01:48:51,650 --> 01:48:59,650
A little pause... and we are back.

